# 8. Backend API Requirements

Use the existing API structure and authentication middleware.

Suggested endpoints:

### Pricing Configuration

- `POST /api/v1/pricing/configurations`
- `GET /api/v1/pricing/configurations`
- `GET /api/v1/pricing/configurations/:id`
- `PATCH /api/v1/pricing/configurations/:id`
- `PATCH /api/v1/pricing/configurations/:id/status`

Admin-only modifications.

### Estimate Management

- `POST /api/v1/estimates`
- `GET /api/v1/estimates`
- `GET /api/v1/estimates/:id`
- `PATCH /api/v1/estimates/:id`
- `POST /api/v1/estimates/:id/recalculate`
- `GET /api/v1/estimates/:id/history`

Implement only the endpoints required by the approved workflow.

### Authorization

- Customers can access only their own estimates.
- Contractors can access only estimates they are authorized to manage.
- Admins can access estimates according to their administrative permissions.
- Only authorized roles can modify pricing configurations.
- Backend authorization must enforce ownership and access restrictions.

