1. Material costs and coverage rates.
2. Service rates and calculation methods.
3. Labor rates and labor calculation methods.
4. Waste percentages.
5. Minimum job price.
6. Travel charges and distance calculation rules.
7. Equipment and additional charges.
8. Tax rules and applicable locations.
9. Monetary rounding rules.
10. Estimate validity period.
11. Estimate approval and rejection workflow.
12. Whether material prices can vary by location or contractor.

Until confirmed, use clearly labeled test fixtures or configuration records marked as sample data. Do not present sample estimates as real commercial quotes.

